<title>JAPAN: Mori Denki down on new share issuance news.</title>
<headline>Mori Denki down on new share issuance news.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Mori Denki Manufacturing Co Ltd were down in afternoon trade after the firm said it would issue eight million new shares in a third party allotment to Shinshin Shoji K.K. president Shodai Nitta, brokers said.</p>
<p>At 0434 GMT, the shares were down 65 yen at 530 yen.  </p>
<p>Mori Denki said on Thursday that it had agreed on a business and equity tie-up with shopping centre operator Shinshin Shoji.</p>
<p>Mori said the issue price of the new shares would be 415 yen per share and the number of outstanding shares after the issue would total 30.20 million.</p>
<p>As Nitta already holds 1.2 million shares, he would become Mori's largest shareholder after the issue, with a 30.5 percent stake, it said.</p>
</text>
